<title>JAPAN: Japan utilities compile plans for new power plants.</title>
<headline>Japan utilities compile plans for new power plants.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese utilities plan to construct the following new power plants, according to data compiled by the Ministry of International Trade and Industry and released on Thursday.</p>
<p>The plans will be presented to a government panel during the fiscal year ending March 1998. The panel will then vote on whether to approve them.</p>
<p> Operator    Capacity	 Start-up	     Fuel type</p>
<p>		(10,000Kw)</p>
<p> TEPCO	   60.0	    July 2001	    fuel oil/</p>
<p>							coal-water-mixture</p>
<p> TEPCO	   60.0	    July 2003	    fuel oil/</p>
<p>							coal-water-mixture</p>
<p> TEPCO	  152.0	    July 2001		LNG</p>
<p>				     July 2002</p>
<p>				     Jan  2003</p>
<p> TEPCO	  152.0	    July 2001		LNG</p>
<p>				     July 2002</p>
<p>				     Jan  2003</p>
<p> TEPCO	  150.0	    July 2002		LNG</p>
<p>				     Nov  2002</p>
<p>				     Mar  2003</p>
<p> TEPCO	  150.0	    July 2009		LNG</p>
<p>				     Nov  2009</p>
<p>				     Mar  2010</p>
<p> Chubu	  100.0	    Nov  2001		coal</p>
<p> Chubu	  100.0	    Nov  2002		coal</p>
<p> Chubu	  100.0	    Nov  2003	    fuel oil</p>
<p> Kansai	 148.0	    Nov  2004		LNG</p>
<p>				     Nov  2005</p>
<p> Kansai	 222.0	FY2007/8 or after	  LNG</p>
<p> Kansai	 110.0	    Jan  2007	orimulsion/fuel oil</p>
<p> Kansai	 110.0	FY2007/8 or after  orimulsion/fuel oil</p>
<p> Kansai	 110.0	FY2007/8 or after  orimulsion/fuel oil</p>
<p> Kansai	 110.0	FY2007/8 or after  orimulsion/fuel oil</p>
<p> Okinawa	 10.3	    May  2000	   crude oil</p>
<p> EPDC	     2.0	    Apr  2000	   geothermal</p>
<p>NOTE: TEPCO is Tokyo Electric Power Co Inc, Chubu is Chubu Electric Power Co Inc, Kansai is Kansai Electric Power Co Inc, Okinawa is Okinawa Electric Power Co Inc and EDPC is Electric Power Development Co Ltd.</p>
